{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XraiwRMDtfXUkh9EaMQjjU","type":"tool_result","content":"title:\tGate, change-set, watchdog and cross-process write lock\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#7\nblocking:\tuser/delegate#12\nnumber:\t9\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nGround-truth verification and safety in the supervisor.\n\n- `--gate CMD` on `run`: the supervisor runs the gate after the agent; a failing gate downgrades DONE to DONE_WITH_CONCERNS and records the gate's output.\n- The git change-set computed by the tool, and the concern when commits landed but the tree is still dirty.\n- `--tool-idle-ms N`: the idle watchdog kills a job that goes silent past the model-idle or tool-idle window (defaults from the host profile) and reports it.\n- A lock file per resolved `cwd`, held by a read-write job's supervisor. A second read-write job in the same `cwd` returns BUSY with the holder's job id, including from another process. Read-only jobs take no lock.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Gate pass and gate fail are reflected in the terminal record.\n- [ ] The change-set lists what the agent changed and committed.\n- [ ] A silent fake agent is killed after the window and the record says why.\n- [ ] Two `delegate run` processes writing the same `cwd`: the second gets BUSY; the lock is released when the first finishes or dies.\n- [ ] End-to-end tests cover each case.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #7 Tracer: delegate run + supervisor + watch on cursor\n     908 /tmp/pr23.diff\nsrc/cli.rs\nsrc/finalize.rs\nsrc/job_registry.rs\nsrc/lib.rs\nsrc/lock.rs\nsrc/status_record.rs\nsrc/types.rs\ntests/cli_e2e.rs","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04a0345a-7eae-4364-9c93-6be8627e4fed","uuid":"bba72af4-1537-4b46-97e2-0437e6a952bc","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:27:13.332Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"title:\tGate, change-set, watchdog and cross-process write lock\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#7\nblocking:\tuser/delegate#12\nnumber:\t9\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nGround-truth verification and safety in the supervisor.\n\n- `--gate CMD` on `run`: the supervisor runs the gate after the agent; a failing gate downgrades DONE to DONE_WITH_CONCERNS and records the gate's output.\n- The git change-set computed by the tool, and the concern when commits landed but the tree is still dirty.\n- `--tool-idle-ms N`: the idle watchdog kills a job that goes silent past the model-idle or tool-idle window (defaults from the host profile) and reports it.\n- A lock file per resolved `cwd`, held by a read-write job's supervisor. A second read-write job in the same `cwd` returns BUSY with the holder's job id, including from another process. Read-only jobs take no lock.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Gate pass and gate fail are reflected in the terminal record.\n- [ ] The change-set lists what the agent changed and committed.\n- [ ] A silent fake agent is killed after the window and the record says why.\n- [ ] Two `delegate run` processes writing the same `cwd`: the second gets BUSY; the lock is released when the first finishes or dies.\n- [ ] End-to-end tests cover each case.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #7 Tracer: delegate run + supervisor + watch on cursor\n     908 /tmp/pr23.diff\nsrc/cli.rs\nsrc/finalize.rs\nsrc/job_registry.rs\nsrc/lib.rs\nsrc/lock.rs\nsrc/status_record.rs\nsrc/types.rs\ntests/cli_e2e.rs","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
