{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbHB3hsCo6dzmSXtuY7g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES\n\nP2 tests/cli_e2e.rs:819 — `silent_agent_stalls_and_record_says_why` only covers the model-idle window, and it gets there through a new `DELEGATE_IDLE_MS` env var. Nothing tests `--tool-idle-ms` killing a silent job. The `SLOW` fake already starts a tool call and then goes quiet. Add a test using `--tool-idle-ms 300` with `SLOW` that expects STALLED.\n\nP2 src/cli.rs:324 — `DELEGATE_IDLE_MS` is undocumented and exists only for tests. Model-idle has no flag, which is consistent with the spec, but the env var is a new production surface. Document it next to `DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS`, or inject the window another way.\n\nP3 src/finalize.rs:106 — the concern text tells the caller to \"pass allowPartialCommit\". #4 removes that parameter. Drop the sentence.\n\nP3 src/cli.rs:52 — `--tool-idle-ms 0` is accepted. That kills any tool call at once and gives the gate a 0 ms timeout. Require a value greater than 0.\n\nP3 src/lock.rs:338 — `DefaultHasher` output is not guaranteed stable across Rust versions. A rebuilt binary can compute a different lock path, so a running job's lock goes unseen. Use a fixed hash (for example FNV).\n\nP3 src/lock.rs:382 — the holder id is written after the lock is taken, and the file is truncated first. A contender can read it in between and print `BUSY ` with no id. Write the id before releasing the window, or retry the read.\n\nP3 src/cli.rs:223 — `settle_dead_supervisor` checks the pid alone. A reused pid hides a dead supervisor. Ruling 7 says stale-heartbeat handling, so also check heartbeat age.\n\nSTATUS: DONE"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2155,"cache_read_input_tokens":59260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2155},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04a0345a-7eae-4364-9c93-6be8627e4fed","uuid":"00d2d764-658f-4898-b90e-8881e41b01d7","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:27:49.685Z","request_id":"req_011CfbHB3JYzKRV8XRHBJVtA"}
