c/cli.rs:324 — `DELEGATE_IDLE_MS` is undocumented and exists only for tests. Model-idle has no flag, which is consistent with the spec, but the env var is a new production surface. Document it next to `DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS`, or inject the window another way.\n\nP3 src/finalize.rs:106 — the concern text tells the caller to \"pass allowPartialCommit\". #4 removes that parameter. Drop the sentence.\n\nP3 src/cli.rs:52 — `--tool-idle-ms 0` is accepted. That kills any tool call at once and gives the gate a 0 ms timeout. Require a value greater than 0.\n\nP3 src/lock.rs:338 — `DefaultHasher` output is not guaranteed stable across Rust versions. A rebuilt binary can compute a different lock path, so a running job's lock goes unseen. Use a fixed hash (for example FNV).\n\nP3 src/lock.rs:382 — the holder id is written after the lock is taken, and the file is truncated first. A contender can read it in between and print `BUSY ` with no id. Write the id before releasing the window, or retry the read.\n\nP3 src/cli.rs:223 — `settle_dead_supervisor` checks the pid alone. A reused pid hides a dead supervisor. Ruling 7 says stale-heartbeat handling, so also check heartbeat age.\n\nSTATUS: DONE","ttft_ms":1858,"type":"result","duration_ms":51149,"uuid":"301a831c-0580-4233-8d4b-48791008a7ac","ttft_stream_ms":1186,"time_to_request_ms":385,"first_content_frame_ms":1186,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
